{# ===========================================================================
   Component: plate

   THE NAP strip on every location page. One file, included by
   tajima-convoy.njk, tajima-college-heights.njk and location-stub.njk, which
   until now each hand-built their own copy and had already drifted: College
   Heights carried no Order row at all and no Menu row, Convoy carried Order
   but no Menu, and the stubs carried both. That drift is the reason this is a
   component now.

   HIERARCHY, 2026-09-14. The previous strip was nine labelled fields in one
   uniform wrapping row, every one at the same weight, and it read as a spec
   sheet. Nothing in it was wrong; nothing in it was prioritised either, and
   the page's conversion action ("Order online") rendered as plain text in a
   metadata field, indistinguishable from "Lot parking".

   Three tiers now, in the order someone actually needs them:

     1. .plate__head   Where it is, whether it is open, how to reach it.
                       Address, hours with the live status, phone. Larger
                       type, and the phone is a real tel: link at a size you
                       can hit with a thumb.
     2. .plate__act    How to order. One real button, the page's primary CTA.
                       Directions sits beside it as a secondary action,
                       because "how do I get there" is the other thing a
                       person does with this strip.
     3. .plate__more   Everything else, kept in full but quieted: parking,
                       seating, happy hour, menu. Label and value on one line
                       each, small, as a group rather than as four peers of
                       the address.

   EVERY FIELD SURVIVES. This is a hierarchy change, not a cull. The rows that
   are conditional are conditional on data, not on which template included
   this: parking is null at Maui, happy hour is gated on the room having a
   bar, and the order link is gated only because the guard costs nothing.

   All values come from locations.json. Nothing here is hardcoded per page.
   =========================================================================== #}

{%- set hh = (happyHour.locations | where("id", loc.id)) | first %}

<address class="plate">

  {# ---------------- 1. Where, when, and how to reach it ---------------- #}
  <div class="plate__head">
    <div class="plate__item plate__item--lead">
      <span class="plate__label">Address</span>
      <span class="plate__value plate__value--lead">{{ loc.address.street }}, {{ loc.address.locality }}, {{ loc.address.region }} {{ loc.address.postalCode }}</span>
    </div>

    {% include "components/plate-hours.njk" %}

    <div class="plate__item plate__item--lead">
      <span class="plate__label">Phone</span>
      <a class="plate__value plate__value--lead plate__tel" href="{{ loc.phone | telHref }}">{{ loc.phone }}</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  {# ---------------- 2. The actions ----------------
     The order button is the page's primary CTA and the only red in this
     strip. The header's Order Online pill is the other red in the viewport,
     which is why Directions next to it is an outlined secondary and not a
     second filled button: two filled reds side by side would be the "more
     than one primary CTA competing" failure DESIGN_SYSTEM.md names.

     Order routes STRAIGHT TO TOAST from locations.json, not via
     /order-online/, which would ask someone to pick the location they are
     already reading about. All seven have a URL; the guard stays because it
     costs nothing. #}
  <div class="plate__act">
    {%- if loc.orderUrl %}
    <a class="plate__order" href="{{ loc.orderUrl }}" rel="noopener">
      Order online<span class="u-visually-hidden"> from {{ loc.name }}</span>
      <svg width="15" height="15" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M1 7H13M13 7L7.5 1.5M13 7L7.5 12.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round"/>
      </svg>
    </a>
    {%- endif %}
    <a class="plate__directions" href="{{ loc | mapsUrl }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
      Directions<span class="u-visually-hidden"> to {{ loc.name }}, opens in a new tab</span>
      <svg width="11" height="11" viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M5 1.5h7.5V9M12.5 1.5 5.5 8.5M9 12.5H1.5V5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
    </a>
  </div>

  {# ---------------- 3. The rest, kept and quieted ----------------
     Label and value read as one line here rather than stacking, because at
     this size a stacked pair costs two lines to say "Street parking". #}
  <div class="plate__more">
    {%- if loc.parking %}
    <span class="plate__fact">
      <span class="plate__label plate__label--inline">Parking</span>
      <span class="plate__value plate__value--quiet">{{ loc.parking }}</span>
    </span>
    {%- endif %}
    <span class="plate__fact">
      <span class="plate__label plate__label--inline">Seating</span>
      <span class="plate__value plate__value--quiet">Walk in. No reservations.</span>
    </span>
    {#
      HAPPY HOUR gated on the room having a bar. Plaza Bonita is quick-serve
      with no alcohol (CLIENT_FACTS.md), so pointing that room at a page about
      drinking would be the link contradicting the room. Maui is not in
      happyHour.json at all, and its brief forbids cross-linking it into the
      San Diego set. The row links, it does not state a time: windows are
      unconfirmed everywhere, which is what /happy-hour/ itself says.
    #}
    {%- if hh and hh.servesAlcohol %}
    <span class="plate__fact">
      <span class="plate__label plate__label--inline">Happy hour</span>
      <a class="plate__value plate__value--quiet" href="/happy-hour/">See times</a>
    </span>
    {%- endif %}
    <span class="plate__fact">
      <span class="plate__label plate__label--inline">Menu</span>
      <a class="plate__value plate__value--quiet" href="/menu/">See the menu</a>
    </span>
  </div>

</address>
